            "review_title": "Review at Apero Bar & Bistro",
            "review_text": "karng\n305 contributions\n0\nMuted Flavors\nJul 2026 • Solo\nBlack Bean Crab Linguine - The pasta was cooked nicely al dente, but the sauce was overly salty, making each bite less enjoyable. I also wished the black bean flavor had been more emphasized.\n\nSpring Onion Focaccia - The interior was pleasantly fluffy and chewy, but the crust lacked the crispness I was hoping for. The spring onion tasted more like a garnish than a key ingredient, so I would have liked its flavor to be more prominent throughout the bread. The accompanying sauce did not complement the bread.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten September 3, 2026",
